            <span class="organ_pill">LEGAL FRAMEWORK</span>
            <h1>Laws & Regulatory Reports on Organ Donation</h1>
            <p>Statutory guidelines, Acts of Parliament, and transplantation policies in India and globally</p>
        </div>

        <div class="about_hero_card" style="text-align: left; margin-bottom: 25px;">
            <h2 style="color: #0369a1; margin-bottom: 12px;">Transplantation of Human Organs and Tissues Act (THOTA), 1994</h2>
            <p style="color: #334155; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 15px;">
                In India, organ donation is strictly regulated by the <strong>Transplantation of Human Organs and Tissues Act, 1994</strong> and its subsequent amendments. The act regulates the removal, storage, and transplantation of human organs and tissues for therapeutic purposes and categorically prohibits any commercialization of organ donation. Organ donation must be voluntary, altruistic, and without monetary incentive to the donor or family.
            </p>
            <p style="color: #475569; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem;">
                The Act establishes Authorization Committees at state and national levels (NOTTO, ROTTO, SOTTO) to oversee hospital licensing, approve living donor relationships, monitor transparency, and combat illegal commercial dealings.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="organ_details_grid" style="margin-bottom: 25px;">
            
            <div class="organ_detail_card">
                <div class="card_header_bar" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0284c7 0%, #0369a1 100%);">
                    <h2>Global Legal Models</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="card_body">
                    <p><strong>United States:</strong> Governed by the National Organ Transplant Act (NOTA) and coordinated by UNOS/OPTN to prevent commercialization and optimize matching networks.</p>
                    <p><strong>European Union:</strong> Governed by the EU Directive on Quality and Safety of Human Organs Intended for Transplantation.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="organ_detail_card">
                <div class="card_header_bar" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e11d48 0%, #be123c 100%);">
                    <h2>Addressing Challenges & Scarcity</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="card_body">
                    <p><strong>Shortage of Donors:</strong> The global demand for donor organs substantially exceeds supply. Awareness drives and donor pledges bridge this critical gap.</p>
                    <p><strong>Anti-Trafficking Safeguards:</strong> Rigorous biometric registry systems ensure human rights protection and absolute transparency.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>

